+# ADR-003: Measurable latency, loss and recovery objectives
+
+Date: 2026-10-05. Status: PROPOSED numbers for owner confirmation (D11). No latency, throughput, RPO or RTO has been measured in Phase A.
+
+## Measurement contract
+
+Use milliseconds for latency, seconds for age/recovery and UTC timestamps. Each eligible sample has a trace/correlation ID, aggregate identity, committed revision/event key, start timestamp, terminal timestamp and outcome. Do not put order IDs, phone numbers, names, tokens, URIs or report rows in metric labels or logs. Detailed trace evidence, if necessary, stays in restricted test artifacts with synthetic IDs only.
+
+`event-to-visible` starts at the source transaction's durable commit (Mongo revision+outbox or PG business state+outbox). It ends when the authoritative API returns the expected revision and the visible active browser screen renders that same revision/totals. Record API and browser endpoints separately; an SSE hint, HTTP 202, submitted provider mutation, cached row or task acknowledgement is not “visible”. For intake, also measure valid raw request/SQS accept start→durable ownership and provider-origin event time→visibility when the approved provider timestamp exists. Report the latter as NOT MEASURABLE when the provider omits that timestamp; never replace it with our receipt time.
+
+Use a local single-node Mongo replica set and fresh isolated PG `_test` databases, fake provider endpoints and fake Meta. Emit synthetic correlated events at a declared rate, wait for a steady warm-up, gather at least 10,000 successful samples per flow for p99, then run declared bursts and fault/restart cases separately. Record nearest-rank p50/p95/p99, sample count, time window, event rate, eligible/excluded/error counts and backlog at start/end. Report pending/timeout outcomes as failures rather than dropping them from percentiles; show age of outstanding events. No error or schema-rejected input belongs in “successful latency”, but rejection and unresolved-effect rates must be reported. Cold-start/replay latency is a separate distribution.
+
+## Proposed flow targets
+
+These are engineering budgets, not claims about existing performance. Owner must approve a realistic workload and provider restrictions; Phase F later establishes supported capacity. Initial Phase B measurement envelope: a bounded steady stream without backlog growth, test-stack resources recorded, and for notification acceptance no more than 0.5 eligible messages/sec/tenant with bursts of at most 20. If that envelope is unrealistic, revise sender capacity/policy/targets before approval. No arbitrary production-volume assumption is hidden here.
+
+| ID / flow | Start → end evidence | p50 / p95 / p99 target | Hard age or lag objective | Reason / real bottleneck |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| S01 Mongo SKU/party/channel/location change → approved PG projection and visible master/central screen | Mongo source revision commit → PG projection revision → correct GET + DOM | 0.5s / 2s / 5s | Projection age ≤10s during healthy operation | Proposed outbox trigger+poll allows subsecond wakeup; current path absent. `api/skus.js`, `inventory/central-api.js`, `inventory/workers.js` proposed projector; 1.5s UI debounce in `src/hooks/useInventoryLiveUpdates.tsx`. |
+| S02 Mongo price/tax/PO/ASN metadata change → affected authorized screens | Owner revision commit → same revision/snapshot visible; no assumed PG pricing write | 0.5s / 2s / 5s | Cache age ≤10s | Dedicated `api/tax*.js`, `api/pricing-events.js`, `api/purchase-orders.js`, `api/manage-asn.js`; require explicit reload/projection contract, not arbitrary broadcast. |
+| S03 GRN receipt authorization → ledger receipt and committed Mongo GRN screen | Durable requested receipt/digest → exact `ci_inventory_event` IDs → GRN committed projection + DOM | 0.5s / 2s / 5s | Pending receipt age ≤15s healthy | Proposed asynchronous replacement for `api/inbound-create-edit.js`/`api/inbound-realtime.js` and `inventory/wms-operations.js`; include both directions, not just PG commit. |
+| S04 Shopify/Woo valid webhook → Unified Orders visible | Request receipt/accepted commit → expected `ci_unified_order` revision and lines + DOM | 0.3s / 2s / 5s | Accepted-intake visibility ≤10s | Direct `recordIncomingOrder` runs in ingress transaction; SSE hook debounce/refetch adds cost. `inventory/ingress.js`, `inventory/http.js`, `src/pages/UnifiedOrders.tsx`. |
+| S05 Amazon accepted SQS order → Unified Orders visible | SQS receive timestamp → committed receipt/order → expected GET + DOM | 0.5s / 3s / 8s | Received-message local visibility ≤15s | `inventory/sqs-worker.js`, separate `scripts/inventory-amazon-sqs.mjs`; queue availability/remote event age tracked separately. A 20s long-poll setting is not evidence that every delivered message waits 20s. |
+| S06 Eligible physical intake → every line reserved and visible stock/timeline | Accepted eligible order revision → all `ci_reservation` rows + ledger events + UI | 1s / 3s / 10s | Unreserved eligible intake age ≤15s healthy | One-second idle inventory worker polling in `scripts/inventory-worker.mjs`; multi-line mapping/lock cost. Observational/report/custody intake is excluded by declared policy, not presented as reserved. |
+| S07 Ledger change → channel quantity submitted | Ledger commit version → actual provider submission for same or newer desired balance/mapping | 1s / 5s / 15s | Oldest eligible unsubmitted balance ≤30s healthy | `inventory/ledger.js`, `inventory/workers.js publishStockTask`, provider quota in `inventory/rate-limit.js`. Submitted is not confirmed. |
+| S08 Ledger change → channel-observed target confirmed | Ledger commit → approved provider readback at same/newer version matches target | 2s / 15s / 60s | Maximum acceptable unconfirmed stock-publish lag **60s** healthy | Readback needs complete contract per provider. Current Shopify safety reconciliation runs every 15 minutes; it alone cannot meet 60s confirmation. Amazon confirmed readback is not implemented here. |
