+| S12 Shopify recovery poll → order visible | Approved provider update timestamp → first successful poll/order commit + DOM | 35s / 80s / 120s | Recovery-feed age ≤120s healthy | Worker schedules observation every 60s; overlap 5m, first lookback 30d, caps 5,000 orders and 100 lines in `inventory/shopify-orders.js`. Phase B must reconcile eligible recovered orders; current poll does not reserve/cancel. |
+| S13 Authorized order/programme report → observed order/association visible | Upload transaction accepted → matching order/parent association/stock observation + DOM | 1s / 5s / 15s | Accepted file visibility ≤30s for declared row limit | `inventory/meesho-orders.js`, `inventory/sales-programs.js`. Measure processing latency separately from file age/report export staleness; reports are not live feeds. Programme stock never implies physical posting. |
+| S14 Approved return QC / immediate transfer → stock and associated screens visible | PG transaction commit → exact receipt/pair ledger IDs, balance + DOM; optional Mongo projection tracked separately | 0.5s / 2s / 5s | Projection completion ≤10s healthy | `inventory/return-service.js`, `inventory/wms-operations.js`; does not cover unimplemented STO in-transit or carrier workflows. |
+| S15 Lost UI hint → correct screen after reconnect/poll | Missed notify/SSE disconnect → authoritative revision loaded + DOM | 30s / 65s / 75s | Stale active screen ≤75s with functioning fallback | `src/hooks/useInventoryLiveUpdates.tsx`/`src/pages/UnifiedOrders.tsx`/`src/pages/LiveOrderWorkspace.tsx` currently use 60s fallback. This is a degraded refresh target, not the healthy 5s event-to-visible target. |
+| S16 Stock drift / failed checkpoint → visible diagnosis | Injected source discrepancy → `ci_channel_stock`/cursor review classification exposed | 60s / 5min / 15min | Safety-net stock drift diagnosis ≤15min until B/C redesign | Existing 15-minute `reconcileShopifyStock` in worker; no complete cross-store reconciler yet. This safety-net budget must not be confused with the 60s stock-publish SLO. |
+
+Flipkart automated order visibility, offline import processor, full PO→putaway and order→pick/pack/carrier lifecycle targets are **BLOCKED / NOT MEASURABLE** until D06/D09 contracts exist. Proposed once authorized: healthy event-to-visible 1s/3s/10s and maximum pending stage age 30s, with physical human/carrier time measured separately. No local implementation currently earns that target.
+
+## Reliability and recovery targets for approval
+
+| Objective | Proposed number and measurement | Limits / concrete owner |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Acknowledged source-event loss | **0 lost acknowledged events**: every successful ingress receipt, approved command or committed ledger event must resolve to a deduped effect or explicit held/rejected/uncertain state after restart/replay. Measure acknowledged count vs durable resolved/pending/review IDs. | Needs transactional Mongo outbox and PG consumer receipts in ADR-002. Counts alone cannot prove no loss; identities/digests must match. Provider events never received/acknowledged are outside local RPO and need subscription recovery evidence. |
+| Local acknowledged-write RPO | **0 acknowledged writes lost for process crash** with durable local test-store settings; verify abort/restart/commit boundaries. | Not a backup or host-loss guarantee. Single-node replica set tests cannot prove production high availability or storage durability under host loss. |
+| Infrastructure disaster RPO | Draft **≤5 minutes** of committed business data under full store/host loss, with matched restore/checkpoints across both stores. | Production backup/PITR/offsite capability unknown. User describes a free shared Atlas tier with backups off; this was not independently verified and cannot be assumed to meet RPO. Phase I must verify documentation/owner tier facts and measure restore on `_test` stack. |
+| Worker crash RTO | **≤60s** from crash detection to worker running again; **≤180s** to reclaim or explicitly classify pre-crash leased work without duplicates. | `scripts/inventory-worker-supervisor.mjs` restart policy; inventory/WhatsApp leases use 2 minutes. “Process up” and “effects recovered” are separate clocks. NOT measured. |
+| Local DB transient-outage RTO | **≤60s** after Mongo/PG becomes healthy to successful owner-store operations; **≤5min** to settle the declared capped test backlog or record review-required effects. | `api/mongo-connection.js` retry cap ~30s with jitter; `reliability/postgres-connection.js`; worker retry schedules can delay beyond target today. Need monotonic, bounded measurement; retries are not proof. |
+| Provider outage recovery | **≤10min** after provider recovers for eligible backlog under the approved capacity envelope; uncertain notification outcomes are review-bound, not automatically retried to claim recovery. | Retry caps currently reach 1 hour. An eventual capped retry is not compatible with 10min without explicit recovery wakeup policy or owner-adjusted target. |
+| Disaster RTO | Draft **≤60 minutes** to restore stores, validate ledger/reservations/receipt links and resume safe read/write service; provider publishing held until reconciliation confirms baseline. | Phase I full timed restore drill required. No timing evidence exists in this phase. |
+| Ready-service availability | Draft **99.9% per rolling 30 days**, separately for authenticated read, business write acceptance and worker effect completion. | Render liveness (`/api/health/live`) only establishes process survival. Strict readiness (`/api/health/ready`) and actual business outcome counters are required. Provider failure is separately attributed, not silently excluded. |
+| Replay and receipt retention | Draft **90 days** durable events/consumer receipts, and business-effect keys for the full business record retention period. | Owner approves legal/PII/deletion constraints and worst provider redelivery interval; never delete dedupe while associated effects can be replayed. |
+
+## SLO failure semantics
+
+Backlog, held conflicts, auth/credential failure, degraded store and uncertainty must be visible independently from success latency. A poison event held for review is loss-free preservation, but it fails the flow latency target; do not count it as successful delivery. During store failure accept no unpersisted writes, return the owner-store unavailable error and show last-confirmed stale data explicitly. Health liveness still survives while readiness may fail.
+
+Stock-publish age >60s needs operator-visible unsafe/stale classification and an account-specific selling/publishing response approved in D03/D11; do not invent an automated remote zero-stock call or a provider suspension capability. Alerts >60s queued need diagnosis of backlog/quota/eligibility; accepted without delivery >120s is delivery-stale and never an instruction to resend blindly. Disconnected UI must expose stale state and successful authoritative refresh must be measured before clearing it.
+
+Phase B records propagation latency on the disposable stack, Phase E fault recovery, Phase F capacity, Phase G metrics/alerts, and Phase I RPO/RTO restore evidence. This ADR defines how to measure those outcomes; none of those later phases has begun.
