+Table roles: `ci_inventory_event` is the immutable physical effect record; `ci_inventory_balance` is its transaction-maintained current state; `ci_channel_stock` and `ci_stock_observation` are provider target/evidence; `ci_unified_order*`, `ci_order_line_state`, `ci_order_timeline` and `ci_reservation` belong to the order/ledger boundary; `ci_return_*` owns approved physical return receipts; `ci_alert_*`, `ci_order_alert*`, `ci_recipient_verification` and WhatsApp cutover tables belong to alert administration/delivery; `ci_program_*`/`ci_sales_program` hold parent associations and custody observations; `ci_connection_*`, `ci_channel_account`, `ci_channel_mapping`, `ci_agent_pairing` belong to connection setup; `ci_ingress`, `ci_outbox`, `ci_sync_*`, `ci_service_heartbeat` are delivery/operational state; `ci_catalog_source_row`, `ci_import_batch` are import evidence; `ci_auth_session` and `ci_login_rate_limit` are auth state. The respective source files above are the real writers/readers. No general-purpose `ci_event_receipt`, Mongo domain outbox, PG picklist/bin/shipment domain tables or approved offline order adapter exist in this inspected schema; those remain proposals.
